  "content": {
    "title": "How to Watch THE PLAYERS Championship This Weekend: The PGA's Flagship Event on NBC & Peacock",
    "text": "How to Watch THE PLAYERS Championship This Weekend: The PGA's Flagship Event on NBC & PeacockThe last couple of weekends on the PGA Tour have been nothing short of spectacular, with two fantastic finishes that went down to the wire (or in last weekend's case, past the wire). But with THE PLAYERS Championship, the PGA Tour's flagship event, coming to NBC and Peacock this weekend, there's plenty more action in store.From Thursday through Sunday, the world's best golfers, including World No. 1 Scottie Scheffler and World No. 2, last year's PLAYERS champ Rory McIlroy, will be converging on one of the most prestigious courses the PGA Tour has to offer, the Pete Dye-designed Stadium Course at Tournament Players Club Sawgrass (TPC Sawgrass for short) in the Jacksonville, Florida area of Ponte Vedra Beach, where the tourney has been held since 1982.If either Scheffler or McIlroy can conquer the course, including its iconic 17th hole island green, they'll join the legendary Jack Nicklaus as the only three-time winners of THE PLAYERS Championship. Here's what you need to know about how to catch the incredible weekend coverage on NBC and Peacock!RELATED: Who Won the PGA Players Championship 2025? Everything to KnowHow to watch THE PLAYERS Championship PGA Tour golf tournament this weekend?NBC Sports’ coverage of THE PLAYERS Championship on NBC and Peacock, live from the from TPC Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, Florida, begins with Round 3 coverage at 2 p.m. ET on Saturday, March 14, and Final Round coverage at 1 p.m. ET on Sunday, March 15. Golf Channel has coverage of the rest of the tourney, which kicks off on Thursday, March 12.What to know about THE PLAYERS Championship this weekend on NBC & PeacockRory McIlroy of Northern Ireland poses with THE PLAYERS Championship 2025 trophy.The 2026 PLAYERS Championship is the 52nd edition of the prestigious event, which features the highest single-event purse on the PGA Tour at $25 million. Not only does the winner get the bulk of that, but also 750 FedExCup points, a three-year invitation to The Masters, and three-year exemptions for the other Majors: the U.S. Open, the Open Championship (aka the British Open) and the PGA Championship.Last year's tourney saw McIlroy defeating J.J. Spaun (who would later go on to win the U.S. Open) in a three-hole Monday playoff, the first three-hole playoff in a decade. Having won THE PLAYERS in 2019, McIlroy became one of just eight golfers to win it multiple times, including Scheffler, who won it back to back in 2023 and 2024, the first and only time a golfer successfully defended his title in PLAYERS Championship history. Scheffler and McIlroy lead a field of 123 top golfers, including 46 of the World Top 50. Other big names participating include Tommy Fleetwood (No. 3), Collin Morikawa (No. 4), Justin Rose (No. 5), Russell Henley (No. 6), Chris Gotterup (No. 7), Robert MacIntyre (No. 8), Sepp Straka (No. 9), and Xander Schauffele (No. 10). And don't count out World No. 19 Akshay Bhatia, who miraculously won the Arnold Palmer Invitational last weekend in a sudden-death playoff.RELATED: Everything to Know About PGA Star Scottie Scheffler: Family, Career & MoreNBC Sports on NBC & PeacockThe biggest games, biggest stars and teams you love are all on NBC and Peacock.NBC and Peacock are home to the NFL with Sunday Night Football, the NBA on NBC and the MLB with Sunday Night Baseball. NBC and Peacock are also the place to find the Olympics, marquee events like the Kentucky Derby, Premier League soccer, and some of the biggest golf tournaments of the year featuring the biggest stars in the sport.Find it all on NBC and Peacock.Who are the announcers for NBC Sports’ coverage of THE PLAYERS Championship PGA Tour event?A view of the 17th hole at the players championshipNBC Sports’ broadcast team for THE PLAYERS Championship includes Dan Hicks and Terry Gannon on play-by-play, veteran analysts Kevin Kisner and Brad Faxon, on-course reporting from Jim “Bones” Mackay, Smylie Kaufman, and John Wood, and interviews by Cara Banks.NBC Sports doesn't just feature the best PGA commentators, but also the best coverage, including its first use of four drone cameras in a golf telecast, offering unique aerial perspectives, augmented reality visuals, and live tracing. NBC Sports' award-winning coverage will also feature Weather Applied Metrics, dedicated bunker cams and drone cams at the 16th and 17th hole, a side follow camera at the 17th tee, robotic reverse-follow camera tracing shots at the 18th tee, fixed-wing airplane coverage from above the Stadium Course, X-mo and super-slo-mo replays, and “NBCeeIt” zoom technology.Following THE PLAYERS Championship, NBC Sports’ PGA Tour coverage continues with the Valspar Championship (March 21-22), Texas Children’s Houston Open (March 28-29), and Valero Texas Open (April 4-5).Did You Know MLB Is Back on NBC and Peacock?The MLB is back on NBC and Peacock this season with the addition of Sunday Night Baseball in primetime and plenty of Peacock-exclusive games on the slate this season. Find the full schedule right here.The line-up features plenty of storied rivalries from across the league. Sunday Night Baseball will be home to division rivalry games including Diamondbacks-Dodgers (March 26); Braves-Phillies (April 19); Tigers-Royals (May 10); Rangers-Angels (May 24); Cubs-Cardinals (May 31); Mets-Phillies (June 21); Yankees-Red Sox (June 28); Padres-Dodgers (July 5); Mariners-Astros (August 16); and Padres-Giants (Sept. 13). Catch it all on Peacock right here.",
